{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up","id":1128421,"title":"[2E] Creating Hosts from the ground up","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-13T06:48:36-07:00","id":1128421,"title":"[2E] Creating Hosts from the ground up","content":"It's possible I'm just completely blind and can't find it in the 2E WtF book, but are there rules for building Hosts? If not, is everyone just using/adapting the info from Predators [1E]?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12962-warlokk","name":"WarLokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T07:44:30-07:00","id":1128437,"title":"","content":"It's a bit of both, but there are basic rules for statting out Shartha. I relied entirely on 2nd Ed rules ( plus a little home brewing to give the Shartha a Shadow Potency esque Power Stat )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T08:21:24-07:00","id":1128446,"title":"","content":"As one that made like 4 or 5 Hosts using Predators, I can't understate my fondness for that book or Shartha, but nowadays I go for 2E rules. The last one I made, the Bat Host, are 2E and I gotta admit it simplifies things while not taking away much and, if I ever manage to keep my word, I'm gonna rework the others into 2E as well.<br /> <br /> The suggestion I can give you is to look at modular powers across the books (like the Horror rules in the book) and take them as basis. For all my efforts and delusions, I won't hide the fact it's easier than it seems. The structure of evolution of metamorphosis of Predators is still valuable and I always keep it in mind<br /> <br /> (The homebrew to give them a Shadow Potency esque Power Stat is totally a good idea, by the way. I always considered the Shartha &quot;almost shapechangers&quot; and it fits)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 08-13-2017, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T09:29:23-07:00","id":1128486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1128446#post1128446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As one that made like 4 or 5 Hosts using Predators, I can't understate my fondness for that book or Shartha, but nowadays I go for 2E rules. The last one I made, the Bat Host, are 2E and I gotta admit it simplifies things while not taking away much and, if I ever manage to keep my word, I'm gonna rework the others into 2E as well.<br /> <br /> The suggestion I can give you is to look at modular powers across the books (like the Horror rules in the book) and take them as basis. For all my efforts and delusions, I won't hide the fact it's easier than it seems. The structure of evolution of metamorphosis of Predators is still valuable and I always keep it in mind<br /> <br /> (The homebrew to give them a Shadow Potency esque Power Stat is totally a good idea, by the way. I always considered the Shartha &quot;almost shapechangers&quot; and it fits)</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, though I will say I was more than a little disappointed with how the Shartha seemed to lost a mechanical method of actually infestating them in true Spirit Host fashion regarding Aspect/ Dread Powers. I guess they use Manifestations now like ephemeral beings.. but that sort of sucks and I don't like it.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the Hosts ability to mutate and evolve is something I keep with my Shartha too. That reminds me, I never got your thoughts on the Host I made, I want to hear what the Shartha Guru has to say on them xD<br /> <br /> ( And yeah, I call it Cohesion to reflect their ever growing progress to being &quot; Whole&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 08-14-2017, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-13T12:41:37-07:00","id":1128547,"title":"","content":"Shartha weren't ephemeral beings to begin with. They're physical entities, from rat or spider form all the way to giant rat or giant spider form. So they get Dread Powers, which are very versatile.<br /> <br /> We could certainly use more information regarding antagonists but the powers that be seem to turn a blind eye to Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T08:35:30-07:00","id":1128843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1128486#post1128486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the Hosts ability to mutate and evolve is something I keep with my Shartha too. That reminds me, I never got your thoughts on the Host I made, I want to hear what the Shartha Guru has to say on them xD<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Probably happened when I took a long hiatus from the forums some time ago. I forced myself to stop being a lurker just recently, but I don't remember reading them indeed or throwing it a like as I'd probably would have done if that was the case.<br /> <br /> Can you give me a link to the thread? Would not call myself <i>the </i>Shartha Guru, but I sure am willing to give you an opinion","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T12:21:42-07:00","id":1128909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1128843#post1128843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably happened when I took a long hiatus from the forums some time ago. I forced myself to stop being a lurker just recently, but I don't remember reading them indeed or throwing it a like as I'd probably would have done if that was the case.<br /> <br /> Can you give me a link to the thread? Would not call myself <i>the </i>Shartha Guru, but I sure am willing to give you an opinion</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem, it happens. Anyway, here it is; perhaps you'll take a liking to them xD<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/884923-gisilu-the-ant-host\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/884923-gisilu-the-ant-host\"> Gisilu: The Ant Host. - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/884923-gisilu-the-ant-host\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/884923-gisilu-the-ant-host </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Hey all, it's been awhile since I have offered content to the Werewolf forum, and I felt that you all would appreciate these little monsters; they have taken a </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T14:01:36-07:00","id":1131870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1128909#post1128909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No problem, it happens. Anyway, here it is; perhaps you'll take a liking to them xD<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/884923-gisilu-the-ant-host\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...u-the-ant-host</a></div> </div> </div> </div>So I, uh, <i>may</i> have gone a little overboard. Your work on the Ant Host and the concept of Cohesion inspired me, and I pumped out this monstrosity. I'm still on the fence about whether I want Shartha to use &quot;proper&quot; Manifestations or just redo a couple appropriate Manifestations as Dread Powers and have done with it. Shards need to be able to infest host bodies <i>somehow</i> after all. I'm also wobbling on whether consuming someone for Essence just does straight Lethal damage or does Aggravated damage like when a werewolf does it.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> <i>Shattered Gods- The Hosts</i><br /> <br /> Remnants of ancient gods slain by Father Wolf for trespassing in the Flesh instead of remaining in the Border Marches, the Hosts gestated out of spilled divine ichor and decaying ephemeral flesh. Along with the Uratha, they are all that remains of lost Pangaea, but the Hosts are verminous and unintended side effects of a god\u2019s death, whereas the Uratha are intentional creations of two gods. The Hosts are represented with a modified version of the Ephemeral Being rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Cohesion</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Trait Max</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Attributes</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Essence/Turn</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Dread Powers</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Manifestations</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4-6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">10/1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1-3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">6-8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">11/2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1-3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9-12</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">12/3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3-5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">11-14</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">13/4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3-5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">15-20</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">15/5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5-7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">20-25</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">20/6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5-7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">12</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">26-31</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">25/7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7-9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">12</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">30-35</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">30/8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7-9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">15</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">36-41</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">50/10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9-11</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">6</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">15</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">40-45</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">75/15</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9-11</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">6</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <i>Verminous Swarm</i>: The Hosts slowly accumulate around themselves swarms of potential vessels for the essence of their Pangaean progenitor, presenting as a Swarm (as per the Swarm Tilt) with a radius equal to Cohesion. In this form, Attributes are only really relevant for the use of Dread Powers that require them, Social or Mental rolls, Clash of Wills, and grappling opponents. The Host shard is treated as possessing Health equal to Resistance + Cohesion.<br /> <br /> <i>Willpower</i>: The Shartha do not possess Anchors like a Virtue or Vice. Instead, like a Spirit, they regain a point of Willpower for every three points of Essence they gain. They can also regain Willpower through rest.<br /> <br /> <i>Regaining Essence</i>: The Hosts can regain Essence through a Locus, but <i>also </i>through consuming the flesh of humans, werewolves, and other Hosts at a rate of one point per Lethal Damage.<br /> <br /> <i>Devouring</i>: When killing (and eating) a character with their natural weaponry the Host spends a point of Willpower and rolls Strength + Resolve (Power + Resistance if in Swarm form). When they run out of Willpower, or achieve successes equal to the other character\u2019s Cohesion/Primal Urge (a Host can generally only consume another Host of the same type or a Werewolf). If successful, the devourer gains one Experience per dot of Cohesion/Primal Urge. They also gain a new Dread Power <i>or </i>an Attribute dot.<br /> <br /> <i>Manifestations</i>: Host cannot possess the Twilight Form Manifestation, as they are solid beings. All Hosts start with the Discorporation and Possess Manifestation, using the Claim Manifestation to become the dreaded Shartha Hybrids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 08-20-2017, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T14:21:12-07:00","id":1131880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1128446#post1128446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As one that made like 4 or 5 Hosts using Predators, I can't understate my fondness for that book or Shartha, but nowadays I go for 2E rules. The last one I made, the Bat Host, are 2E and I gotta admit it simplifies things while not taking away much and, if I ever manage to keep my word, I'm gonna rework the others into 2E as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda confused here, what rules for creating Host? I am looking at the 2nd Forsaken Core and the only thing i can find is a 2 NPC examples.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T14:48:31-07:00","id":1131888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1131880#post1131880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kinda confused here, what rules for creating Host? I am looking at the 2nd Forsaken Core and the only thing i can find is a 2 NPC examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's on page 203, on the right side, bottom half.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T09:39:29-07:00","id":1132244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1131870#post1131870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I, uh, <i>may</i> have gone a little overboard. Your work on the Ant Host and the concept of Cohesion inspired me, and I pumped out this monstrosity. I'm still on the fence about whether I want Shartha to use &amp;quot;proper&amp;quot; Manifestations or just redo a couple appropriate Manifestations as Dread Powers and have done with it. Shards need to be able to infest host bodies <i>somehow</i> after all. I'm also wobbling on whether consuming someone for Essence just does straight Lethal damage or does Aggravated damage like when a werewolf does it.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> <i>Shattered Gods- The Hosts</i><br /> <br /> Remnants of ancient gods slain by Father Wolf for trespassing in the Flesh instead of remaining in the Border Marches, the Hosts gestated out of spilled divine ichor and decaying ephemeral flesh. Along with the Uratha, they are all that remains of lost Pangaea, but the Hosts are verminous and unintended side effects of a god\u2019s death, whereas the Uratha are intentional creations of two gods. The Hosts are represented with a modified version of the Ephemeral Being rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\"><b>Cohesion</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\"><b>Trait Max</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\"><b>Attributes</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\"><b>Essence/Turn</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\"><b>Dread Powers</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\"><b>Manifestations</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">4-6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">10/1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">1-3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">6-8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">11/2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">1-3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">9-12</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">12/3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">3-5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">11-14</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">13/4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">3-5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">15-20</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">15/5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">5-7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">20-25</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">20/6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">5-7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">12</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">26-31</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">25/7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">7-9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">12</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">30-35</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">30/8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">7-9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">15</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">36-41</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">50/10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">9-11</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">6</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">15</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">40-45</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">75/15</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">9-11</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"padding: 0px\">6</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <i>Verminous Swarm</i>: The Hosts slowly accumulate around themselves swarms of potential vessels for the essence of their Pangaean progenitor, presenting as a Swarm (as per the Swarm Tilt) with a radius equal to Cohesion. In this form, Attributes are only really relevant for the use of Dread Powers that require them, Social or Mental rolls, Clash of Wills, and grappling opponents. The Host shard is treated as possessing Health equal to Resistance + Cohesion.<br /> <br /> <i>Willpower</i>: The Shartha do not possess Anchors like a Virtue or Vice. Instead, like a Spirit, they regain a point of Willpower for every three points of Essence they gain. They can also regain Willpower through rest.<br /> <br /> <i>Regaining Essence</i>: The Hosts can regain Essence through a Locus, but <i>also </i>through consuming the flesh of humans, werewolves, and other Hosts at a rate of one point per Lethal Damage.<br /> <br /> <i>Devouring</i>: When killing (and eating) a character with their natural weaponry the Host spends a point of Willpower and rolls Strength + Resolve (Power + Resistance if in Swarm form). When they run out of Willpower, or achieve successes equal to the other character\u2019s Cohesion/Primal Urge (a Host can generally only consume another Host of the same type or a Werewolf). If successful, the devourer gains one Experience per dot of Cohesion/Primal Urge. They also gain a new Dread Power <i>or </i>an Attribute dot.<br /> <br /> <i>Manifestations</i>: Host cannot possess the Twilight Form Manifestation, as they are solid beings. All Hosts start with the Discorporation and Possess Manifestation, using the Claim Manifestation to become the dreaded Shartha Hybrids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well done! I'm glad my little pet project someone to make such a useful table for these mechanics. I don't know about anyone else, but I would definitely use this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T12:30:45-07:00","id":1132356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1132244#post1132244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very well done! I'm glad my little pet project someone to make such a useful table for these mechanics. I don't know about anyone else, but I would definitely use this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank-you! High praise! Any suggestions as to whether the Hosts should be able to inflict Aggravated Damage by feeding for Essence? Also, nifty little thing they can do with the mechanics. If a Host in Swarm Form grapples a werewolf, condenses in on them, and manages to keep hold, they could conceivably make it easy-ish to kill them, especially since the average werewolf has no way to harm a Swarm. Also, if they choose to inflict harm while Grappling, then they can theoretically overwhelm a werewolf quickly enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T13:43:23-07:00","id":1132379,"title":"","content":"Instead of Cohesive I would simply use (<b>CoD Rulebook</b>) Horror's Potency or Rank as name for Hosts Power Stat, but that's me.<br /> <br /> To help dot those Hosts, we made with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24\" data-vbnamecard=\"24\">Mr Gone</a> - a while ago - Predators sheet for 2E, for running Urged and Hosts with it especially. Maybe handy - or may need some changes by you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/WtF/WtF_2ndED_Predators_2-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/WtF/WtF_2ndED_Predators_2-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/WtF/WtF_2ndED_Predators_2-Page_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\"> https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/WtF/WtF_2ndED_Predators_2-Page_Interactive.pdf </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T04:07:25-07:00","id":1138543,"title":"","content":"As I running now story about Beshilu in modern Sweden - Maybe we could recreate those with above fan rules? In 2E corebook there is only write-up for Red Minister, sadly, even if book mentions few other monsters in Beshilu Nests:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WtF 2E, p. 203</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Watch out for the Ministers. They\u2019re like Beshilu alphas or royalty, the high priests of rat-kind. They\u2019re crazy but they\u2019re smart, and they\u2019ve got some sort of ability to fuck with other shards too \u2014 not just eating them, but chewing them up and spitting them out. That\u2019s why we keep seeing all sorts of freaky <b>new Beshilu like those tank-sized tunnellers</b>, and <b>the vomit-spitters</b> the Bright Lights ran into last week. The Ministers are walking, talking manifestations of the worst horror stories of GMO bullshit.</div> </div> </div> </div>So let's write up classical Rat Swarm, those <b>Tunnellers</b> and <b>Vomit-Spitters</b>. Also, from <i><b>Predators</b></i> book, we have those...<br /> <br /> <b>Gnawers:</b> Beshilu in their still-formative rat stages - mostly human govern by one to few Host Shards.<br /> <br /> <b>Rokhan: </b>Evolved Beshilu, perhaps fused with human hosts.<br /> <br /> How many Cohesion would have those? I probably see something like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Cohesion 1-3: Gnawer<br /> Cohesion</b> <b>4-6: <i>Rokhan</i></b><br /> <b>Cohesion </b><b>7+ : <i>Minister<br /> <br /> Tunnellers </i></b>and <b><i>Vomit-Spitters</i></b>, as alternative 'evolutions', would probably be at Cohesion 4-6, probably?<br /> <br /> Simple Rat Swarm would only have Cohesion and <i>Verminous Swarm Power?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-09-2017, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T11:16:02-07:00","id":1138646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1138543#post1138543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I running now story about Beshilu in modern Sweden - Maybe we could recreate those with above fan rules? In 2E corebook there is only write-up for Red Minister, sadly, even if book mentions few other monsters in Beshilu Nests:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So let's write up classical Rat Swarm, those <b>Tunnellers</b> and <b>Vomit-Spitters</b>. Also, from <i><b>Predators</b></i> book, we have those...<br /> <br /> <b>Gnawers:</b> Beshilu in their still-formative rat stages - mostly human govern by one to few Host Shards.<br /> <br /> <b>Rokhan: </b>Evolved Beshilu, perhaps fused with human hosts.<br /> <br /> How many Cohesion would have those? I probably see something like this:<br /> <br /> <b>Cohesion 1-3: Gnawer<br /> Cohesion</b> <b>4-6: <i>Rokhan</i></b><br /> <b>Cohesion </b><b>7+ : <i>Red Minister<br /> <br /> Tunnellers </i></b>and <b><i>Vomit-Spitters</i></b>, as alternative 'evolutions', would probably be at Cohesion 4-6, probably?<br /> <br /> Simple Rat Swarm would only have Cohesion and <i>Verminous Swarm Power?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Very nice, though I have a minor nitpick; not all the Ministers are called Red Minister. Unless I misunderstood and you were just giving Red Minister a Conhesion score, and I'm sorry","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T00:18:48-07:00","id":1138819,"title":"","content":"Okay, I fixed that thing with Ministers. Still, let's fix on doing something.<br /> <br /> <b>Let's start with proverbial <i>Rats Swarm</i></b> - How much Cohesion? They stats as Ephemerals ( i.e. Power, Finesse, Resistance etc. )? What Dread Powers this Rat Swarm could have?<br /> <br /> On my eye, for <b><i>Rats Swarm</i></b>:<ul><li>Cohesion 1, 2 in <i>very </i>big groups</li> <li>Works as Ephemerals ( cause writing Manipulation or Resolve for big crowd of rats will be problematic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</li> <li>Dread Power are Verminous Swarm, Beastmaster and Venomous Ichor ( if have enough slots on them on last one ).</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-09-2017, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T11:55:06-07:00","id":1139238,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a>, where is Swarm Tilt written in official books? I try to hammer simple Beshilu Rats and have problem to see where are rules to what you are adresing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T13:40:54-07:00","id":1139263,"title":"","content":"Found the rules for Swarm Tilt in <b>DtD</b> corebook...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DtD, p. 179</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>SWARM (ENVIRONMENTAL) </b><br /> Animals of Size 1 are generally best represented by swarms, flocks and other groupings of the animals. Swarms are measured by their radius in yards. A swarm inflicts one point of bashing damage to anyone within its radius. A swarm can inflict more damage by condensing. Every time the swarm condenses to cover half of its full area, it inflicts one additional point of damage per turn. Therefore, a swarm of eight yards in radius inflicts two bashing damage per turn if it constricts down to a four-yard radius, three bashing if it halves that again to a two-yard radius, and four bashing damage per turn it if condensed itself down to a one-yard radius. Though condensing doesn\u2019t usually happen all that often in nature (save in the case of creatures such as killer bees), it is an easy enough thing for a being with supernatural powers to command them to do so.<br /> Armor is effective against a swarm only if it covers one\u2019s full body, but even then it provides only half its rating. In addition, targets are distracted by the swarm, suffering \u20132 dice on all rolls while they are within the radius, even if they\u2019re not specifically attacked.<br /> <b>Causing the Tilt:</b> The Swarm Exploit can cause this Tilt, as can similar powers from non-demonic sources. The Tilt can occur naturally if someone disturbs a nest of bees.<br /> <b>Ending the Tilt:</b> The swarm cannot be attacked with fists, clubs, swords or guns. Only area-affect attacks such as a torch affect it. Each point of damage inflicted by a flame or other applicable attack halves the swarm\u2019s size. Once the swarm is reduced below a one-yard radius, either all insects are dead or the few remaining disperse.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>My Comment on Swarm Tilt with Hosts:</b> To relate them more to Ephemeral Beings rules, I would simply make that Swarm\u2019s Size is it\u2019s radius - and that \u2018condensing\u2019 of Swarm is lowering their Size ( and thus Health ), but adds damage bonus. I think it simply could work as Manifestation for Hosts, instead of Twilight Form. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-10-2017, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T14:00:12-07:00","id":1139271,"title":"","content":"So here is my first proposition for Beshilu Host...<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Rats Swarm</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>&lt;Scratching sounds in the walls&gt;</i></span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Shartha are spreading by spiritual shards infecting living animals that are descended from their Pangean progenitor \u2013 Plague King. In the first phase of Beshilu intrusion, shards are spreading in rats nest population, leading some of vermins in it to sustain shards until full grown up in rats bodies. When mature, individual shards are separating from nest and biting humans to spread the Host. Till then, they are all living in rats swarms that gnaw the Gauntlet \u2013 and humans \u2013 in underground and dark places. All seems to follow the single mind, governed by the shard in their midst.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Few dozens of filthy rats, doing actions like from one mind \u2013 until meet other Beshilu shard, then two groups fights for control over colony. Or they evolve further, when finding suitable human body they can Claim.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Rat Swarm is looking for places to hide and spread. Once finding perfect place for rats, it multiplies and growing next Bashilu shards in it\u2019s midst. All the time they are gnawing the Gauntlet, letting lose next spirits to split in to world of Flesh. When colony is spread enough and shards are mature, Swarm starts to seek human host \u2013 or abduct some to bite into them. It\u2019s most often around Size 8-10 of the Swarm.<br /> <br /> <b>Notice:</b> Rats Swarm is using traits as Ephemeral Being, but is totally physical ( well, physical rats that are spiritual infected ). Instead of Rank it has Cohesion, working more or less the same for it as Rank for Spirits. Rats Swarm is, obviously, under Swarm as Manifestation instead of Twilight Form and follows rules for Swarms Tilt in it. It\u2019s Size is Swarm radius and he can halve it for extra damage. Even if normal attacks of Swarm are only Bashing damage, each of them is spreading Moderate Poisoned Tilt on it\u2019s victims from Venomous Ichor \u2013 adding each turn 1 Bashing damage if not resisted \u2013 but as Uratha have inner resistance to Toxins ( they omit number of points equal to their Primal Urge ), it\u2019s not very helping rats here.<br /> <br /> <b>Cohesion: </b>1<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 3, Finesse 2, Resistance 4<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 10<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 9<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Discorporate, Possess, Swarm<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Beastmaster (Rats), Gnaw Gauntlet, Venomous Ichor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-11-2017, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T18:08:58-07:00","id":1139312,"title":"","content":"Why does it have manifestations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T21:23:34-07:00","id":1139349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1139312#post1139312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does it have manifestations?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's because <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> fan rules on Hosts have Manifestation. Only novelty to them is that I use Swarm as one of Manifestatins and swap Twilight Form of normal Ephemera for Hosts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1131870#post1131870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I, uh, <i>may</i> have gone a little overboard. Your work on the Ant Host and the concept of Cohesion inspired me, and I pumped out this monstrosity. I'm still on the fence about whether I want Shartha to use &quot;proper&quot; Manifestations or just redo a couple appropriate Manifestations as Dread Powers and have done with it. Shards need to be able to infest host bodies <i>somehow</i> after all. I'm also wobbling on whether consuming someone for Essence just does straight Lethal damage or does Aggravated damage like when a werewolf does it.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> <i>Shattered Gods- The Hosts</i><br /> <br /> Remnants of ancient gods slain by Father Wolf for trespassing in the Flesh instead of remaining in the Border Marches, the Hosts gestated out of spilled divine ichor and decaying ephemeral flesh. Along with the Uratha, they are all that remains of lost Pangaea, but the Hosts are verminous and unintended side effects of a god\u2019s death, whereas the Uratha are intentional creations of two gods. The Hosts are represented with a modified version of the Ephemeral Being rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Cohesion</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Trait Max</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Attributes</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Essence/Turn</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Dread Powers</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Manifestations</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4-6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">10/1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1-3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">6-8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">11/2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1-3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9-12</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">12/3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3-5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">11-14</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">13/4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3-5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">15-20</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">15/5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5-7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">20-25</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">20/6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5-7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">12</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">26-31</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">25/7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7-9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">12</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">30-35</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">30/8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7-9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">15</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">36-41</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">50/10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9-11</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">6</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">15</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">40-45</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">75/15</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9-11</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">6</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <i>Verminous Swarm</i>: The Hosts slowly accumulate around themselves swarms of potential vessels for the essence of their Pangaean progenitor, presenting as a Swarm (as per the Swarm Tilt) with a radius equal to Cohesion. In this form, Attributes are only really relevant for the use of Dread Powers that require them, Social or Mental rolls, Clash of Wills, and grappling opponents. The Host shard is treated as possessing Health equal to Resistance + Cohesion.<br /> <br /> <i>Willpower</i>: The Shartha do not possess Anchors like a Virtue or Vice. Instead, like a Spirit, they regain a point of Willpower for every three points of Essence they gain. They can also regain Willpower through rest.<br /> <br /> <i>Regaining Essence</i>: The Hosts can regain Essence through a Locus, but <i>also </i>through consuming the flesh of humans, werewolves, and other Hosts at a rate of one point per Lethal Damage.<br /> <br /> <i>Devouring</i>: When killing (and eating) a character with their natural weaponry the Host spends a point of Willpower and rolls Strength + Resolve (Power + Resistance if in Swarm form). When they run out of Willpower, or achieve successes equal to the other character\u2019s Cohesion/Primal Urge (a Host can generally only consume another Host of the same type or a Werewolf). If successful, the devourer gains one Experience per dot of Cohesion/Primal Urge. They also gain a new Dread Power <i>or </i>an Attribute dot.<br /> <br /> <i>Manifestations</i>: Host cannot possess the Twilight Form Manifestation, as they are solid beings. All Hosts start with the Discorporation and Possess Manifestation, using the Claim Manifestation to become the dreaded Shartha Hybrids.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-10T22:24:50-07:00","id":1139358,"title":"","content":"Is it me or Gnaw Guanlet should GENERATE Essence, not costing it? Cost on this instinctual to Beshilu action seems counter to this Host lore from Predators book... \ud83d\ude15","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T00:57:27-07:00","id":1139371,"title":"","content":"<b>Comment:</b> Doing some more Beshilu NPCs I see that using for Corpus sum Cohesion + Resistance is surely to low. Changed stats to work with normal for spirits Resistance + Size.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Rats Nest</b></span><br /> &lt;Scratching sounds and faint squirms in deep tunnels&gt;<br /> <b>Background: </b>Rat Nest is when multiple Beshilu Swarms are collecting in one dreadful colony, spanning thousands upon thousands of rats, more or less under one mind. Most often it\u2019s Minister ruling it, but some rare occasions pointed to coherent lesser Shards of Plague King agreeing on common idea to put down Gauntlet.<br /> <b>Description:</b> Thousands upon thousands of rats, with some more intelligent individual inside colony. The sight of full Nest alone is reason for Integrity Breaking Point roll for most humans.<br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Rat Nest is almost always creating itself for one purpose of Beshilu race at large \u2013 bringing down the Gauntlet. With numbers alone of normal rats under lead of Shards in it\u2019s amidst \u2013 it gnaws the barrier between Worlds of Flesh and Spirit in matter of day, maybe two. Following are various disease- and plague-spirits, spreading from Nest site to all local Territories of many packs.<br /> <br /> <b>Cohesion: </b>3<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 4, Finesse 2, Resistance 6<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 12/3<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 2<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Size:</b> 20<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 26<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Claim, Discorporate, Possess, Swarm<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Beastmaster (Rats), Gnaw Gauntlet, Home Ground ( Nest site ), Natural Weapons (1), Venomous Ichor","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-11-2017, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T07:38:44-07:00","id":1139434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1139358#post1139358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it me or Gnaw Guanlet should GENERATE Essence, not costing it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wearing away at the wall between worlds that interferes with the flow of Essence without actually building the critical mass of Resonance to form a locus doesn't seem to be contradicted by the action not being free. It also mechanically explains why a Rat Host might ever leave their work alone despite being as driven to do it as they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cost on this instinctual to Beshilu action seems counter to this Host lore from Predators book... \ud83d\ude15 </div> </div> </div>Which lore and how?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-11T09:04:37-07:00","id":1139461,"title":"","content":"So, I mucked around with those rules a little more, especially with an eye for the text and mechanics in <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken Second Edition pg. 202-205</b>, and seemed to find a couple of numerical patterns that stand out and allow for a slightly more elegant rewrite. This might be seeing something in nothing, but it works alright for me. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> Cohesion + Resistance is, generally, a decent amount of Health, if only because conventional assault against a Swarm is useless, as per the Swarm Tilt rules. Area of Effect damage behaves normally instead of halving the Swarm, because a Swarm of <i>shartha </i>is very different than a Swarm of natural insects or rats. Because of this, unless your Werewolf is one with Gifts that enable easy access to Area of Effect damage (hello Gift of the Elements, favoured Gift of the Hunters in Darkness), pawing at a Host swarm is effectively useless, and you'll just get yourself bogged down.<br /> <br /> Anyways, here's my rewrite.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> <i>Shattered Gods- The Hosts</i><br /> <br /> The Hosts are the most dangerous prey that any werewolf can hunt. These blasphemous fragments of ancients gods- beings that survived even Father Wolf\u2019s rage -are caught in an eternal effort to forge their progenitors anew from their spiritual shards. They are a foe that can hide, coiled in the carcasses of humanity, and at the same time they are terrible abominations of immense size and strength. They twist the Gauntlet with ease, befouling the two worlds. Just killing a <i>shartha</i> is rarely enough to truly finish it off.<br /> <br /> <b>Essence:</b> The base substance of ephemera is the lifeblood of the Hosts, dictating the limits of their power. A Host shard starts with an Essence of 1, which is also the total number of points of Essence they can hold.<br /> \u00b7 <i>Attributes</i>: A Host in its natural shape possesses the three simplified Attributes Power, Finesse, and Resistance. They possess a number of Attribute dots equal to (Essence + 3), and they infest a victim at the same rate as the Claimed.<br /> \u00b7 <i>Verminous Swarm</i>: The Hosts slowly accumulate around themselves swarms of vessels for the essence of their Pangaean progenitor, presenting as a Swarm (as per the Swarm Tilt) with a radius equal to Essence. In this shape they possess Health equal to Resistance + Essence, though they can divide themselves into multiple, smaller, Swarms if necessary.<br /> \u00b7 <i>Dread Powers</i>: When first infested, a Host only possesses the Discorporation and Gnaw Gauntlet (Beshilu) or Gauntlet Webs (Azlu) Dread Powers. They gain another Dread Power for every three points of Maximum Essence they possess.<br /> \u00b7 <i>Regaining Essence</i>: The Host may gather Essence from Loci, or by devouring the flesh of humans, werewolves, and other <i>shartha</i>. When devouring for Essence they inflict Aggravated damage, but only regain a single point of Essence, regardless of how much damage they would naturally inflict.<br /> <br /> <b>Cohesion: </b>A Supernatural Tolerance Trait representing the <i>shartha</i>\u2019s accumulation of Essence, slowly building into something that is like the dead god from whose corpse they crawled forth. Use the Primal Urge chart on <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken Second Edition pg. 93</b>. When the Host\u2019s maximum Essence increases past the equivalent maximum Essence for that level of Primal Urge, their Cohesion increases.<br /> <br /> <b>Willpower: </b>The Hosts possess neither Virtue nor Vice, instead regaining Willpower only through rest, and through the consumption of Essence. Like Spirits, they regain a point of Willpower for every three points of Essence they regain.<br /> <br /> <b>Devouring: </b>When the Host kills another shard, or a werewolf, they may take the time devouring them utterly, adding their spiritual potency to their own. If they fully consume another Host shard or werewolf (as per Regaining Essence above) then they add the victim\u2019s Primal Urge (or Essence) to their own Essence.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> So, a few things that this does which I consider rather nifty. At high Cohesion/Essence it allows Swarms to get positively <i>enormous </i>instead of just reasonably big. If the Red Minister, as written, was to be killed in their hybrid form, they'd transform into a Swarm with a radius of 20 Yards, or 60-ish feet (not withstanding any reduction in radius due to damage taken that killed the hybrid). And, of course, the Swarm could divide itself up in order to cover the retreat of a fraction of the original Swarm. Risky, but potentially highly rewarding if it allows the Host to survive a werewolf assault. Another thing I noticed is that, following these rules, Cohesion starts out building rather slowly, explodes very quickly in the mid-range, and then slows way down once it hits Cohesion 8. The transformation into something resembling a reformed Pangaean god takes time. Of course, if the Host doesn't mind cannibalizing its own kind, it can build up power a lot more quickly than they would if they went after, say, werewolves exclusively.<br /> <br /> I also did away with Manifestations for the <i>shartha </i>because I realized that the mechanics of inducing a Host infection should really be narrative in scope and really don't <i>need </i>to be written up except for as a short-hand of how long it takes before a fairly regular person warp into a monstrosity. It's up to you whether certain Dread Powers are repressed in Swarm Form and only arise as their host body mutates, or whether they are &quot;on&quot; all the time. Use judgement as necessary. Personally, depending on the Dread Power, I'd have them arise one at a time for every three Attribute dots the target gains, barring the ones they get for free which are always present. Gives the nice, slow, Body Horror slide from freshly dead human to sack of skin filled with rats/spiders, to gigantic, monstrous hybrid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T04:34:44-07:00","id":1139679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1139461#post1139461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> Cohesion + Resistance is, generally, a decent amount of Health, if only because conventional assault against a Swarm is useless, as per the Swarm Tilt rules.<br /> Area of Effect damage behaves normally instead of halving the Swarm, because a Swarm of <i>shartha </i>is very different than a Swarm of natural insects or rats.</div> </div> </div> </div>So untill you can make Area of Effect attack you cannot do ANY damage to <i>Shartha</i> Swarm?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1139461#post1139461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because of this, unless your Werewolf is one with Gifts that enable easy access to Area of Effect damage (hello Gift of the Elements, favoured Gift of the Hunters in Darkness), pawing at a Host swarm is effectively useless, and you'll just get yourself bogged down.</div> </div> </div> </div>But are Cohesion 1 Swarms even enough dengerous to at least 1 Uratha? Cause it all will look like:<br /> <br /> 'Uratha Player: I attack Swarm.<br /> ST: You cannot do any real damage to you. Swarm is condensing, doing +1 Bashing damage. It's 4 Bashings to you.<br /> Uratha Player: Okay, I go for Basu-Im. We go with Down &amp; Dirty Combat now. I have 9 success on attack.<br /> ST: Swarm have 4 success. &lt; Check Cohesion+Resitance and see 5 for starting Swarm. &gt;<br /> Uratha Player: Yay, Swarm is defeated with my Basu-Im!'<br /> <br /> If we add mutliple Uratha characters, sending one Swarm of anything simply does not have any sense. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: In your revised rules you use Essence + Resistance that is <i>much</i> more than Cohesion+Resistance. I think your version with Essence is much more appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-12-2017, 08:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T04:58:09-07:00","id":1139681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1139461#post1139461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Shattered Gods- The Hosts</i><br /> (...)<br /> <br /> <b>Essence:</b> The base substance of ephemera is the lifeblood of the Hosts, dictating the limits of their power. A Host shard starts with an Essence of 1, which is also the total number of points of Essence they can hold.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean here newly born Shard, just running from previous Joined corpses, yes? Cause typical 'I control rat/spider' Shard should have at least a 2-4 Essence points. It's more or less 'small spirit locked in body'.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1139461#post1139461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u00b7 <i>Attributes</i>: A Host in its natural shape possesses the three simplified Attributes Power, Finesse, and Resistance. They possess a number of Attribute dots equal to (Essence + 3), and they infest a victim at the same rate as the Claimed.<br /> \u00b7 <i>Verminous Swarm</i>: The Hosts slowly accumulate around themselves swarms of vessels for the essence of their Pangaean progenitor, presenting as a Swarm (as per the Swarm Tilt) with a radius equal to Essence. In this shape they possess Health equal to Resistance + Essence, though they can divide themselves into multiple, smaller, Swarms if necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so I see the Essence Max Pool is <i>de facto</i> XP Pool of Hosts in your take and Shards slowly evolve with getting Essence. Can work with this, it's elegant way to do it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1139461#post1139461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u00b7 <i>Dread Powers</i>: When first infested, a Host only possesses the Discorporation and Gnaw Gauntlet (Beshilu) or Gauntlet Webs (Azlu) Dread Powers. They gain another Dread Power for every three points of Maximum Essence they possess.</div> </div> </div> </div>No Manifestations, okay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1139461#post1139461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> \u00b7 <i>Regaining Essence</i>: The Host may gather Essence from Loci, or by devouring the flesh of humans, werewolves, and other <i>shartha</i>. When devouring for Essence they inflict Aggravated damage, but only regain a single point of Essence, regardless of how much damage they would naturally inflict.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should not Uratha still give <i>Shartha</i> more Essence? They are the closest to working Pangean shards Hosts want to recreate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1139461#post1139461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Cohesion: </b>A Supernatural Tolerance Trait representing the <i>shartha</i>\u2019s accumulation of Essence, slowly building into something that is like the dead god from whose corpse they crawled forth. Use the Primal Urge chart on <b>Werewolf: The Forsaken Second Edition pg. 93</b>. When the Host\u2019s maximum Essence increases past the equivalent maximum Essence for that level of Primal Urge, their Cohesion increases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice and simple mechanics of Hosts evolution - I like it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1139461#post1139461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Willpower: </b>The Hosts possess neither Virtue nor Vice, instead regaining Willpower only through rest, and through the consumption of Essence. Like Spirits, they regain a point of Willpower for every three points of Essence they regain.</div> </div> </div> </div>With 3 Essence per Willpower point you get like Shard getting 1 WP only after killing 3 humans. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Maybe just make 1 WP for 1 Essence? Or give more Essence from Humans - like maybe Health/2, rounded down?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1139461#post1139461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Devouring: </b>When the Host kills another shard, or a werewolf, they may take the time devouring them utterly, adding their spiritual potency to their own. If they fully consume another Host shard or werewolf (as per Regaining Essence above) then they add the victim\u2019s Primal Urge (or Essence) to their own Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1139461#post1139461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a few things that this does which I consider rather nifty. At high Cohesion/Essence it allows Swarms to get positively <i>enormous </i>instead of just reasonably big. If the Red Minister, as written, was to be killed in their hybrid form, they'd transform into a Swarm with a radius of 20 Yards, or 60-ish feet (not withstanding any reduction in radius due to damage taken that killed the hybrid). And, of course, the Swarm could divide itself up in order to cover the retreat of a fraction of the original Swarm. Risky, but potentially highly rewarding if it allows the Host to survive a werewolf assault. Another thing I noticed is that, following these rules, Cohesion starts out building rather slowly, explodes very quickly in the mid-range, and then slows way down once it hits Cohesion 8. The transformation into something resembling a reformed Pangaean god takes time. Of course, if the Host doesn't mind cannibalizing its own kind, it can build up power a lot more quickly than they would if they went after, say, werewolves exclusively.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Okay, so my Rats Nest example is some powerful Gnawer or starting Rokhan ( Cohesion 3, so circa Essence 12 )?</b> Cause it's not sounds as 'true Nest' to me - it's like 12 Yards radius of rats... And then I understand it's circa (12)^2 square meters of rats, i.e. 144 m2 - Okay, this seems like 'Nest' to work with. Still, I will probably move it more to Cohesion 5-6 to have like 225- 400 m2 of rats - much more looking like 'true Nest' to me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Question to those points - <b>If Shard is in Joined form ( i.e. human-Host hybrid ) does all those rats disappear?</b> Or rather are not under control of Host? So if <i>Beshilu</i> do Joining on some human, then whole Nest simply disappear?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-12-2017, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T05:32:36-07:00","id":1139685,"title":"","content":"Hosts rules, version 2 - <b>How is Defense calculated for Cohesion 1?</b> Lower of Power and Finesses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-12-2017, 08:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T06:03:26-07:00","id":1139690,"title":"","content":"I remade my example <i>Beshilu</i> NPCs with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> 2nd version of rules. I wait to hear what do you think about them...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Rats Swarm</b></span><br /> &lt;Scratching sounds in the walls&gt;<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Shartha are spreading by spiritual Shards infecting living animals that are descended from their Pangean progenitor \u2013 Plague King. In the first phase of Beshilu intrusion, Shards are spreading in rats local population, leading some of vermins in it to sustain shards until full grown up in rodents bodies. When mature, individual Shards are separating from nest and biting humans to spread the Host. Till then, they are all living in Rats Swarms that gnaw the Gauntlet \u2013 and humans \u2013 in underground and dark places. All seems to follow the single mind, governed by the Shard in their midst. This particular Swarm is just before evolution to Cohesion 2 of it\u2019s <i>Beshilu</i> Shard.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Few dozens of filthy rats, doing actions like from one mind \u2013 until meet other <i>Beshilu</i> Shard, then two groups fights for control over colony. Or they evolve further, when finding suitable human body they can Claim. They take more or lest 9 meters radius of rats swarm.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Rat Swarm is looking for places to hide and spread. Once finding perfect place for rats, it multiplies and growing next Bashilu shards in it\u2019s midst. All the time they are gnawing the Gauntlet, letting lose next spirits to split in to world of Flesh. When colony is spread enough and shards are mature, Swarm starts to seek human host \u2013 or abduct some to bite into them.<br /> <br /> <b>Cohesion: </b>1<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 4, Finesse 3, Resistance 5<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 8<br /> <b>Essence/Per Turn:</b> 9/1<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 3<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Size:</b> 9 ( Yards of Radius from Swarm Tilt/Form)<br /> <b>Health:</b> 14<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Beastmaster (Rats), Discorporate, Gnaw Gauntlet, Toxic Bite 2<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Rats Nest</b></span><br /> &lt;Scratching sounds and faint squirms in deep tunnels&gt;<br /> <br /> <b>Background: </b>Rat Nest is when multiple Beshilu Swarms are collecting in one dreadful colony, spanning thousands upon thousands of rats, more or less under one mind. Most often it\u2019s Minister ruling it, but some rare occasions pointed to coherent lesser Shards of Plague King agreeing on common idea to put down Gauntlet for good.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Thousands upon thousands of rats, with some more intelligent individual inside colony. The sight of full Nest alone is reason for Integrity Breaking Point roll for most humans. They take circa 20 yards radius of rats.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Rat Nest is almost always creating itself for one purpose of Beshilu race at large \u2013 bringing down the Gauntlet. With numbers alone of normal rats under lead of Shards in it\u2019s amidst \u2013 it gnaws the barrier between Worlds of Flesh and Spirit in matter of day, maybe two. Following are various disease- and plague-spirits, spreading from Nest site to all local Territories of many packs.<br /> <br /> <b>Cohesion: </b>6<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 7, Finesse 4, Resistance 12<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 21/6<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 16<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 4<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 1/0<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 16<br /> <b>Size:</b> 20<br /> <b>Health: </b>32<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Armored Hide 1, Beastmaster (Rats), Discorporate, Gnaw Gauntlet, Home Ground ( Nest site ), Natural Weapons 2, Toxic Bite 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-12-2017, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T08:00:26-07:00","id":1139706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1128421-2e-creating-hosts-from-the-ground-up?p=1139679#post1139679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Uratha Player: I attack Swarm.<br /> ST: You cannot do any real damage to you. Swarm is condensing, doing +1 Bashing damage. It's 4 Bashings to you.<br /> Uratha Player: Okay, I go for Basu-Im. We go with Down &amp; Dirty Combat now. I have 9 success on attack.<br /> ST: Swarm have 4 success. &lt; Check Cohesion+Resitance and see 5 for starting Swarm. &gt;<br /> Uratha Player: Yay, Swarm is defeated with my Basu-Im!'<br /> <br /> If we add mutliple Uratha characters, sending one Swarm of anything simply does not have any sense. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, the Uratha might win that encounter, but a few dozen dead rats and a fleeing swarm doesn't alleviates the host issue. No, I wouldn't allow down and dirty Basu-Im to completely destroy a swarm as the intent; are you kidding me? Nevermind further collateral damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T09:13:34-07:00","id":1139715,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> alright, so, to answer your questions in order.<br /> <br /> 1- A Host with an Essence of 1 is brand new, a Crawler or Gnawer that just hatched from an Azlu Crone's egg or crawled forth from a Rat King's nest. A Host ready to take a body is, as you say, probably around Essence 2-4. The example &quot;weak&quot; Host in the book is an Azlu of Essence 4. At any given time there's only one &quot;true&quot; Host shard amongst a Swarm, but their Essence is contained in the Swarm in its entirety. It's easier to mechanize it as a Swarm as opposed to dealing with the issue of hopping host body to host body.<br /> <br /> 2- If you're a little concerned about being unable to actually harm a Swarm Form Host (which, by the straight rules on Swarms, you can't if you're using conventional combat techniques) you might want to consider treating them as if they had the Unbreakable Dread Power. Unless the character gains an Exceptional Success then the Swarm only takes a single point of Bashing damage, while with an Exceptional Success they take damage normally. I also wouldn't enable a werewolf in Basu-Im to use Down and Dirty Combat to take down an entire Swarm. A nifty thing you can do to make Hosts more dangerous is have the entire Swarm grapple a target into submission. If they do <i>that </i>then they're safe from potential attack, and also have the potential to inflict more damage than the conventional Swarm Tilt damage. You could also have them devour a target for Essence, which could make even a small Swarm <i>seriously </i>dangerous, even to a werewolf.<br /> <br /> 3- If you <i>really </i>want to you could have the Hosts regain Essence as per the Bound in Mage 2E. So a point of Essence per point of Health, plus any Essence in the target's pool/Pattern, plus a point per dot of Primal Urge/Cohesion. I just used the werewolf rules on regaining Essence from eating flesh. Also, it's important to remember that they regain a point of Essence <i>per attack </i>that deals Aggravated Damage, regardless of how much damage is inflicted. If they eat slowly, reduce the damage inflicted per &quot;bite&quot;, then they can get more Essence out of a target. In which case a Host would get a maximum of <i>two </i>Willpower per entire human (on average) to a maximum of three Willpower per entire human. Note that it's <i>any </i>source of Essence, however, including using a Locus or gaining Essence and/or maximum Essence from eating another Host Shard.<br /> <br /> 4- A Swarm Joining with a human <i>would </i>cause the Swarm to disappear... unless you choose for it not to. Part of the Swarm could remain outside the body, which is easy enough to model since a Host gains an Attribute dot per point of Maximum Essence, which also equates to an extra yard of radius to the Swarm. Just stop the Joining process at a particular point, which divides the Swarm into two pieces. One group is in a Hybrid, another is still a Swarm. This enables a single Host to divide itself, potentially between multiple bodies and/or multiple places. All they have to do is wait for themselves to heal back up if part of the Swarm is destroyed, which means that killing one, or even <i>multiple</i>, Hybrids might not even purge a single Nest.<br /> <br /> I also rather like your example <i>Beshilu</i>. I think it's important to remember that the impact of Toxins using the Toxicity rules on Uratha has no bearing on, say, the Poisoned Tilt as imposed by the Toxic Bite Dread Power. Unless your characters use Gauru liberally, and have no problem with Death Rage, then the Grave Poisoned Tilt will eventually take its toll on them. Even with Gauru they'll have to leave it eventually, and Swarms are stupidly hard to kill. Eventually, the Swarm will win. Adding Natural Weapons on to that adds an extra point or two of Lethal Damage to the inherent damage of the Swarm, and this is still without actively rolling to direct the Swarm to attack with intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T06:04:03-07:00","id":1140498,"title":"","content":"Two hybrids NPCs, based on thought from Arcanist...<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Gnawer \u2013 Blue Collar Worker</b></span><br /> &lt;Nervous ticks coming from broad shoulder man&gt;<br /> - W<i>hat\u2026 do you\u2026 want from\u2026 me?</i><br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Gnawer is one of Beshilu Shards that wormed it\u2019s way to the heart of some pure human, assuming his identity for up to two weeks. Original body host is all that dead, but Rat is wearing his mask and flesh, having only vague flashes of memories or knowledge.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> This particular Gnawer is made from human rather broad shoulder and dressed in working clothes. He was working in some physical job in a bit isolated place like for urban waterworks or on construction site, probably still walking it and protecting nest in nearby.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Gnawer do not have a clue how to work his old job, but his bodies traits let him to pass still as one of workers in simpler tasks. He looks over dangerous for close Beshilu nest and trying to trap next human or werewolves for it\u2019s meal to evolve into proper Rokhan.<br /> <br /> <b>Cohesion: </b>2<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intelligence 2, Wits 2, Resolve 3, Strength 4, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3, Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Crafts 2, Medicine 1, Science 1, Athletics 3, Brawl 2, Larceny 1, Weaponry 1, Animal Ken 1, Intimidation 1,<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 2 (Disease Spirits), Danger Sense, Fast Reflexes 1, Iron Stamina 2, Trained Observer 1<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 11/2<br /> <b>Willpower: </b>6<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8 ( 14 in Swarm form, use stats of Rats Swarm )<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 12<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Beastmaster (Rats), Discorporate, Gnaw Gauntlet, Monstrous Resilience, Venomous Ichor<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Rokhan \u2013 Tunneller</b></span><br /> &lt; Sound of something burrowing and gnashing of teeths in the nearest wall &gt;<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <a href=\"https://t13.deviantart.net/-b7o4LKULkmXxtx9M4dDEhvMhSo=/fit-in/700x350/filters:fixed_height(100,100):origin()/pre00/f4d2/th/pre/i/2016/138/a/9/rat_ogre_charge_by_bra1neater-da2ynt9.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"https://t13.deviantart.net/-b7o4LKULkmXxtx9M4dDEhvMhSo=/fit-in/700x350/filters:fixed_height(100,100):origin()/pre00/f4d2/th/pre/i/2016/138/a/9/rat_ogre_charge_by_bra1neater-da2ynt9.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Rokhan is one of Beshilu Shards that evolved enough to join with human body in monstrous hybrid form of part human, part rat. Tunneller is popular variant of those monsters, made to dig deeper tunnels and passages in underground, preparing place for greater Beshilu Nest, secured from outside world. They also works as bodyguards to the Nest, because of their size and power.<br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Tunnellers are made of biggest human bodies each Nest can find. They are over 3 meters large mountain of muscle and rats fur, often being larger than even most of Gauru forms. They look what truly would like Killer Form if Beshilu would be true shapchangers, not only Host from fragmented Plague King. The sight of Tuneller alone is reason for Integrity Breaking Point roll for most humans.<br /> <br /> <b>Storytelling Hints:</b> Tunellers are not very bright. Most of the time they are pointed at their enemies and just try to rip them in two \u2013 or eat them. But they are incredibly loyal to the Nest that spawn them, not being stopped by even other Beshilu.<br /> <br /> <b>Cohesion: </b>4<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Intelligence 1, Wits 3, Resolve 3, Strength 5, Dexterity 3, Stamina 5, Presence 4, Manipulation 1, Composure 3<br /> <b>Skills:</b> Crafts 2, Athletics 4, Brawl 4, Survival 2, Weaponry 1, Animal Ken 3, Intimidation 4,<br /> <b>Merits:</b> Allies 2 (Nest), Danger Sense, Demolisher 1, Fast Reflexes 1, Giant, Hardy 3, Indomitable, Iron Stamina 3, Trained Observer 1<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 13/4<br /> <b>Willpower: </b>6<br /> <b>Health:</b> 13 ( 23 in Swarm form, use stats of Rats Nest )<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 7<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 7<br /> <b>Armor:</b> 1/0<br /> <b>Size:</b> 8<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 16<br /> <b>Dread Powers:</b> Armored Hide 1, Burrow, Discorporate, Gnaw Gauntlet, Juggernaut*, Regenerate 1<br /> <br /> * I think about giving those Strength bonus to damage rolls in genera, not only on buildings or strictures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-15-2017, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T16:00:46-07:00","id":1258063,"title":"","content":"Coming back to this after a year, I\u2019m very humbled that a pet project of mine took to some people. That makes me very happy to help provide inspiration for people to make into their own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T04:44:24-07:00","id":1378502,"title":"","content":"Seeing with how low mechanical support for Hosts and their mechanical rules give us <b>Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon </b>( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) - I would advise <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> to put his 2E Host rules for the Storyteller's Vault. I gladly would add my NPCs examples to it - and make few more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}